SPEC = {
 "file":"cover_wtw_2027_data_scientist_graduate_programme",
 "label":"WTW 2027 Graduate Data Scientist (London)",
 "p1":"I am writing to apply for the 2027 Graduate Data Scientist programme within Insurance Consulting and Technology in London. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, with A-level Mathematics at A*, Chemistry at A* and Biology at A. Across my academic and professional work I have developed, assessed and deployed machine learning models, written code other people have to run, and presented results to those who had to act on them.",
 "p2":"What attracts me to WTW's ICT team is that the consulting rests on the firm's own technology. Radar and Emblem are used across the market for pricing and, increasingly, for predictive analytics in claims, and with more than 1,200 ICT colleagues in 35 markets a model answers to an underwriting decision rather than to a journal. Pricing, claims and operational processes are data-hungry in the way I enjoy: the data is messy, the target is commercial, and someone downstream has to defend the number.",
 "p3":"The development, assessment and deployment of machine learning models is the core of my MSc dissertation. On 458,840 participants of longitudinal biobank data I engineered multi-timepoint features and compared logistic regression against three tree ensembles, reaching an AUC of 0.714 to 0.718 with near-perfect calibration. For a pricing audience that trade-off is the interesting part: the model separates only moderately, but the predicted probabilities are trustworthy, and I reported both rather than leading with the flattering figure. I assessed robustness with E-values and bias analysis, validated externally, and deployed the work as a Streamlit application for users who had not written the models.",
 "p4":"On machine learning and generative AI, and on using AI tools with a clear view of their limits, this is the substance of my most recent role. For a pharmaceutical client I designed a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension safety rubric with red-line rules, adopted as the acceptance standard for their patient-facing AI. I then built a Python pipeline connecting six large language models with retrieval-augmented generation, scoring more than 2,400 responses through an LLM-as-judge framework, and co-built a knowledge graph whose effect I tested with blinded paired A/B tests. The lesson was where these systems fail, not where they impress. I use Claude Code daily and treat its output as a draft to be checked.",
 "p5":"Presenting analysis internally and to clients is where my consulting experience sits. At Ipsos Strategy3 I structured evidence from more than 80 healthcare professional interviews into quantitative variables and built market-sizing and forecasting models, turning both into client-facing dashboards and recommendations. At TikTok Shop UK I query merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python to explain why commercial performance moved, build the KPI frameworks e-commerce teams use to set targets, and take recommendations to operations, product and commercial colleagues.",
 "p6":"Collaborating across geographies is familiar ground: my pharmaceutical and consumer-technology work was delivered with teams in Hangzhou and Shanghai for clients based elsewhere, and I led a UCL project team building a clinical NLP pipeline. Native Mandarin alongside English has been useful more often than I expected.",
 "p7":"I would bring Python, R and SQL, a statistical foundation that takes calibration and validation seriously, and hands-on experience with generative AI and RAG rather than familiarity from reading. I have no insurance background, so reserving, capital and pricing conventions would be new, and having moved from biology to consumer-technology analytics to health data science in three years, learning a domain quickly is what I have most practice at. I hold the right to work in the UK without sponsorship until January 2029. Thank you for considering my application; I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience fits the programme and the ICT team's work across pricing and claims.",
}
